# Hexproof from [quality] judges the spell as it is (CR 702.11d, 105.2): a source whose color changes changes the
# answer. General Ferrous Rokiric has hexproof from monocolored; Knight of Malice has hexproof from white. On turn 2
# Bot2's Lightning Bolt, red alone, can't target the General, and kills the Ornithopter instead (the positive control).
# On turn 4 Bot2's Painter's Servant enters naming white: every spell is white in addition to its other colors, so the
# next Lightning Bolt is red and white - multicolored, not monocolored. Now it can't target Knight of Malice (a white
# spell), and can target the General, which dies.

